i am having dns  also 

Great 👍 If you already have DNS, you can connect your domain to your server and run your Django app with Nginx + Gunicorn using the domain.

Here is the full process.

1️⃣ Point DNS to Your Server

Go to your DNS provider (like GoDaddy, Namecheap, or Amazon Route 53).

Create an A Record:

Type	Name	Value
A	@	YOUR EC2 PUBLIC IP

Example:

Type: A
Host: @
Value: 43.205.136.192
TTL: 300

For www domain:

Type: A
Host: www
Value: 43.205.136.192

After saving, DNS propagation may take 5–10 minutes (sometimes up to 1 hour).

2️⃣ Update Django ALLOWED_HOSTS

Open settings:

nano ~/My_CRM/crm/settings.py

Change:

ALLOWED_HOSTS = ['yourdomain.com','www.yourdomain.com','43.205.136.192']

Example:

ALLOWED_HOSTS = ['mycrm.com','www.mycrm.com']

Restart Gunicorn:

sudo systemctl restart gunicorn
3️⃣ Update Nginx Configuration

Edit Nginx config:

sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/mycrm

Change server_name:

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name yourdomain.com www.yourdomain.com;

    location / {
        include proxy_params;
        proxy_pass http://unix:/root/My_CRM/gunicorn.sock;
    }

    location /static/ {
        root /root/My_CRM;
    }
}

Test config:

sudo nginx -t

Restart Nginx:

sudo systemctl restart nginx
4️⃣ Open Your Website

Now open:

http://yourdomain.com

Your Django CRM site should load.

5️⃣ Enable HTTPS (Very Important)

Install SSL using Certbot.

Install:

sudo apt install certbot python3-certbot-nginx

Run:

sudo certbot --nginx

Choose your domain.

After that your site will work with:

https://yourdomain.com
