in aws i will use routr 53 sevice

If you want to use Amazon Route 53 to connect your domain to your Django server, follow these exact steps. This will point your domain to your EC2 server where Nginx + Gunicorn + Django are running.

Step 1 — Open Route 53

Login to **Amazon Web Services Console

Search Route 53

Open Hosted Zones

Step 2 — Create Hosted Zone

Click Create hosted zone

Fill:

Domain name: yourdomain.com
Type: Public hosted zone

Click Create hosted zone

You will see 4 Name Servers (NS) like:

ns-123.awsdns-45.com
ns-234.awsdns-67.net
ns-345.awsdns-89.org
ns-456.awsdns-12.co.uk
Step 3 — Update Nameservers in Domain Provider

If you bought the domain from GoDaddy, Namecheap, etc:

Go to domain DNS settings

Replace nameservers with the Route 53 nameservers

Example:

ns-123.awsdns-45.com
ns-234.awsdns-67.net
ns-345.awsdns-89.org
ns-456.awsdns-12.co.uk

Save.

DNS propagation may take 10–30 minutes.

Step 4 — Create A Record in Route 53

Inside your hosted zone:

Click Create Record

Record 1
Record name: yourdomain.com
Record type: A
Value: 43.205.136.192
TTL: 300
Record 2
Record name: www
Record type: A
Value: 43.205.136.192

Now your domain will point to your EC2 server.

Step 5 — Update Django ALLOWED_HOSTS

Open settings:

nano ~/My_CRM/crm/settings.py

Change:

ALLOWED_HOSTS = ['yourdomain.com','www.yourdomain.com']

Restart Gunicorn:

sudo systemctl restart gunicorn
Step 6 — Update Nginx

Open config:

sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/mycrm

Change:

server_name yourdomain.com www.yourdomain.com;

Example:

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name yourdomain.com www.yourdomain.com;

    location / {
        include proxy_params;
        proxy_pass http://unix:/root/My_CRM/gunicorn.sock;
    }
}

Restart Nginx:

sudo systemctl restart nginx
Step 7 — Test Domain

Open browser:

http://yourdomain.com

Your Django site should load.

Step 8 — Enable HTTPS (Recommended)

Install Certbot:

sudo apt install certbot python3-certbot-nginx

Run:

sudo certbot --nginx

Now your site will work with:

https://yourdomain.com
